      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14210400/assets/6dd62794ee072530cd2b6c8028101b58ae617d6757d29f79de90d1a439f6529b.png)\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{(6x-1)f(x)}{5}$ for the function $f(x)$ plotted above.",
      "worked_solution": "We find from the graph that ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=2.$ So we calculate\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{(6x-1)f(x)}{5} & =\\frac{1}{5}(6\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 1}x-1)\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(6(1)-1)(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5} \\\\  & =2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
